    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nWhat is the Three Amigos approach is a QA concept used to evaluate, prevent, or manage software quality. The practical focus is collaboration and fast feedback. QA should participate in refinement, clarify acceptance criteria, identify negative and edge scenarios, prepare test data, test continuously, and help the team understand release risk. Agile does not mean skipping documentation or exploratory testing, and automation is valuable only when it provides reliable feedback. Quality should be part of the team's shared Definition of Done rather than being postponed to the end of a sprint. A strong answer connects the concept to an observable example and explains when it is useful.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis question checks whether you can connect testing practice to risk and release confidence. A strong answer explains what evidence you would collect and why that evidence is sufficient for the scenario.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. What is the Three Amigos approach is a QA concept used to evaluate, prevent, or manage software quality.\n2. The practical focus is collaboration and fast feedback.\n3. QA should participate in refinement, clarify acceptance criteria, identify negative and edge scenarios, prepare test data, test continuously, and help the team understand release risk.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nLead with the distinction that matters most. Then connect it to behavior, a practical consequence, and one limitation.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. What is the Three Amigos approach is a QA concept used to evaluate, prevent, or manage software quality.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn quality engineering, the concept matters when deciding what evidence is needed before release. Test scope should reflect risk, change impact, customer usage, and the cost of missing a defect.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Stopping at the definition without explaining how the concept behaves.\n- Using an example that does not actually demonstrate the point.\n- Making an absolute claim when configuration, version, workload, or context changes the result.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nStay close to the exact question. One technically precise example is more valuable than a broad overview of the entire technology.",
